      "level": 1,
      "ordinal": 7,
      "summary": "These heightened crack spreads reflect the loss of European refining capacity, including the permanent closure of the UK's 220 kbpd Coryton refinery in July, as well as the earlier shutdown of France's 105 kbpd Berre L'Etang refinery. Anticipated refinery closures are also weighing on the product market, as ExxonMobil plans to shut one 80 kbpd crude distillation unit at its 330 kbpd Fawley plant in the UK this month, while ERG will be closing its 89 kbpd Rome refinery this autumn.",
